  "source_component": "src/linker_robot_assets/assets/components/hands/linkerhand_l6",
  "scope": "Standalone source assets and optional six-task environment extension; outside the fixed seven-hand benchmark.",
  "license": "No license file or explicit asset license declaration found in the source checkout; no license inferred from existing L20 assets.",
  "changes": [
    "URDF and MJCF renamed to source.urdf and hand.xml; local simulation and range corrections are listed below.",
    "Variant paths in meta.yaml updated for the destination layout.",
    "Meshes copied without content changes; O6 includes only files referenced by the selected side URDF and MJCF.",
    "MJCF uses implicitfast at 0.002 s and explicit mimic-constraint solver parameters; meshes, body masses, body inertias, and coupling ratios are unchanged.",
    "L6 thumb driver and actuator upper bound reduced to 0.78539768 rad to respect the distal limit at multiplier 1.226495; URDF limits match. Removed redundant sixth polynomial coefficient in the URDF extension.",
    "L6 URDF MuJoCo extension carries the same timestep, integrator, and equality solver settings as hand.xml.",
    "Regression checks: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_linkerhand_assets.py -v (MuJoCo 3.4.0). The standalone MJCF is tested; task composition is implemented separately in dexjoco.extensions.linkerhand.",
    "2026-11-13 contact repair: finite actuator force limits use URDF effort for L6/L30; stricter original O6 MJCF force limits are preserved.",
    "Passive joint damping and friction are copied from source.urdf (zero where absent). Position servos use kp=5 Nm/rad and kv=1 Nm*s/rad; joint armature=0.001 kg*m^2 is numerical regularization, not a measured motor inertia.",
    "Mimic constraints and contact response use solref=0.004 1 at the 0.002 s timestep; contact solimp=0.99 0.99 0.001 0.5 2 and margin=0 m. Hand collision priority=1 keeps these contact parameters against priority-0 scene objects. Geometry, body inertias, mass, joint axes, mimic ratios, and original adjacent-link exclusions are preserved; the added thumb-mount exclusion is described below.",
    "Source URDF effort values are source-model limits, not independently measured hardware specifications. Standalone model tests do not establish six-task benchmark support.",
    "The L6 URDF MuJoCo extension is synchronized with the updated MJCF joint-default and equality settings; its kinematics, effort limits, and standard joint dynamics are retained.",
    "2026-11-13: exclude only hand_base_link versus thumb_metacarpals self-contact for the two-axis thumb mount. Triangle-mesh clearance check across 31x31 roll/pitch configurations per side found no intersections (minimum clearance 0.181 mm), whereas a single convex hull generated false overlap up to several millimeters. Both links retain their object and other-link colliders. Active-joint motion tests now cover every driven axis with contacts enabled.",
    "2026-11-13 task-contact correction: zero contact margin keeps force-bearing contacts on the geometric surface, consistent with shared task contact predicates. No object geometry or success threshold changes.",
    "2026-11-14 integration: optional task environments add a rigid visible/collidable flange bracket while retaining native wrist transforms and hand inertias. Original seven-hand models and task thresholds are unchanged."
  ],
